From: guillermo <guillermo.karsz@solid-run.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 09:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hummingboard-iiot: let the boot LED pattern settle on the final colour

The pattern trigger repeats a device-tree pattern forever. It holds a
brightness only when two consecutive tuples carry the same value; when
the last tuple wraps to the first with a different value it enters the
gradual-dimming branch and re-arms a 50 ms timer for the whole hold
time. The red channel ends and starts at 255, so it holds; the green
and blue channels end at 160 / 90 and start at 0, so the trigger kept a
timer and an I2C write to the LP5562 running every 50 ms on both
channels for the whole uptime (the light looked right, nothing else
did).

Append a zero-length tuple with the hold value to those two patterns.
The hold tuple then wraps to an equal brightness, takes the step branch
and the timer is armed once for the hold time; the trigger skips the
zero-length tuple when the pattern eventually repeats. The visible
sequence is unchanged: red, green, blue, red over four seconds, then
steady white.

Signed-off-by: guillermo <guillermo.karsz@solid-run.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/hailo/hummingboard-iiot.dtsi | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/hailo/hummingboard-iiot.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/hailo/hummingboard-iiot.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/hailo/hummingboard-iiot.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/hailo/hummingboard-iiot.dtsi
@@ -140,7 +140,7 @@
             chan-name = "G";
             label = "G";
             linux,default-trigger = "pattern";
-            led-pattern = <0 1000 255 1000 0 1000 0 1000 160 4294967295>;
+            led-pattern = <0 1000 255 1000 0 1000 0 1000 160 4294967295 160 0>;
             led-cur = /bits/ 8 <0x20>;
             max-cur = /bits/ 8 <0x60>;
             reg = <1>;
@@ -151,7 +151,7 @@
             chan-name = "B";
             label = "B";
             linux,default-trigger = "pattern";
-            led-pattern = <0 1000 0 1000 255 1000 0 1000 90 4294967295>;
+            led-pattern = <0 1000 0 1000 255 1000 0 1000 90 4294967295 90 0>;
             led-cur = /bits/ 8 <0x20>;
             max-cur = /bits/ 8 <0x60>;
             reg = <2>;
